OSQP solves convex quadratic programs with an operator splitting method.
It supports sparse problems, warm starts, matrix updates and infeasibility
certificates. The bundled QDLDL direct solver supplies the factorization.

This package installs the shared C library, public headers and CMake export.
It uses double precision, 64-bit indices and QDLDL 0.1.9. Adjoint derivatives,
profiling, printing and interrupt handling are enabled. Code generation is
disabled. Catch2 and the static upstream test library are not installed.
The upstream library is unversioned; no cross-release ABI is promised.
